      "releaseNotes": "1.0.1: security review fixes (jobId path-traversal guard, UI HTML escaping, server-side one-shot execution confirmation), disclosure corrections, packaged LICENSE + third-party notices, per-connection TLS (off/require/verify), 0600 output files. Round 2 on the same tag: large output files are streamed instead of read whole (a multi-GB rollback script could abort the sidecar), manual stop keeps the generated files and statistics, history view with connection attribution plus per-job delete, panic isolation at the request/engine/exec boundaries, lazy output preview.",
